missing_entities.description:
The room is set up with entities that Home Assistant does not have (any more):

{entities}

Replace or remove them under **Configure** of the room (Settings → Devices & services → Better Media Player). A renamed entity is followed by itself.

disabled_entities.description:
The room is set up with entities that are disabled:

{entities}

Enable them again, or replace or remove them under **Configure** of the room (Settings → Devices & services → Better Media Player).

shared_entities.description:
Several rooms switch or play on the same entities; each would turn them on and off for itself:

{entities}

Every plug, device and player belongs to one room: remove it from the others under **Configure** of the room (Settings → Devices & services → Better Media Player).

group_player.description:
The room's player is a group player:

{entities}

A room needs its own player (a group's queue would be lost). Choose the room's own player under **Configure** of the room (Settings → Devices & services → Better Media Player).

removed_entities.description:
Since this version a room's settings are no longer entities; they are set in the panel or with the action `better_media_player.set_setting` (read with `better_media_player.get_settings`). These removed entities are still used:

{entities}

Change those automations and scripts to the action (see the documentation, Automations). This note goes away once nothing uses them any more.
